---
layout: app-layout.njk
title: Performance Insights – Climbing Logbook
discipline: true
bundle: performance-hub
lowercaseDoctype: true
staticShellNote: |-
  Genuinely static shell (#348, #575) -- hub page for epic #5's
         Performance Insights section. Lists every insight as a tile
         (row-card shape, client/row-card.js); each is its own real
         sub-page. client/performance-hub-main.js reads the username from
         location.pathname itself, same as every other owned page.
---
<div class="max-w-[960px] mx-auto">
  <!-- Picker/menu row before the brand row, and align-left on
       <climbing-header> -- matches /logbook's own layout (left-aligned
       brand row below the header row, not centered above it). Found via
       Raven's production report, 2026-08-10 -- see climbing-header.js's
       own comment on the align-left attribute. -->
  <climbing-page-header></climbing-page-header>

  <div class="flex items-end gap-3 mb-5" id="picker-tabs-row">
    <climbing-discipline-picker></climbing-discipline-picker>
    <climbing-tab-bar active-page="performance"></climbing-tab-bar>
  </div>

  <!-- #599 -- 2 columns on wide screens, matching public/account/index.html's
       own #account-sections grid pattern, 1 column under 600px. -->
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 gap-y-2 max-[600px]:grid-cols-1" id="insight-tiles"></div>

  <div class="text-center text-muted text-[.78rem] mt-8" id="footer"></div>
</div>
